  "body": "> A cookie is script-visible when it is in-scope and does not have the HttpOnly cookie flag.\r\n\r\nI notice this definition is only used in informative text. That's good, because it's not very precise (what does \"in scope\" mean?). Probably this should be called out, e.g.\r\n\r\n> A cookie is script-visible when it is in-scope and does not have the HttpOnly cookie flag. This is more formally enforced in the processing model, which consults https://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-httpbis-rfc6265bis-03#section-5.5 at appropriate points.\r\n\r\nAlso, as a side note, this definition feels kind of lonely, and could probably move to https://wicg.github.io/cookie-store/#cookie-concept. (It's OK to use terms before you define them.)",
